Title:
claude-red — Offensive security skills for Claude (SKILL.md library)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This repository is a curated library of “skills” (structured `SKILL.md` system-prompt files) for the Claude Skills system, aimed at making Claude behave like a context-aware red team specialist per attack surface.  
- It solves the problem of repeatedly re-explaining methodology/tooling by providing drop-in, on-demand prompt modules that load based on conversational triggers.  
- The content spans many offensive domains (web vulns like SQLi/XSS/SSRF, AD/ADCS abuse, EDR evasion, exploit dev, fuzzing, wireless attacks, cloud, CI/CD, containers/K8s, mobile, IoT, and AI security).  
- It includes supporting tooling such as an install script, a JSON manifest (`claude-skills.json`), and conversion/build scripts to manage and index skills.  
- Useful primarily for red teamers, pentesters, bug bounty hunters, and security researchers who want consistent playbooks/checklists embedded into an LLM workflow.  
- Interesting because it operationalizes LLM “prompt engineering” into a maintainable, modular knowledge base with category structure and contribution standards.

Technical Focus:
- Claude Skills system integration via `SKILL.md` system prompts and trigger-based loading  
- Offensive methodology playbooks across web, AD, wireless, cloud, and post-exploitation  
- EDR evasion concepts (e.g., unhooking, indirect syscalls, PPID spoofing)  
- Exploit development and mitigations (ASLR/CFG/CET, ROP, crash triage, TOCTOU)  
- Wireless/IoT attack surfaces (WPA2/3, 802.1X/EAP, BLE, Zigbee, Z-Wave, LoRa/sub-GHz)  
- Repository tooling: installer, manifest generation, skill indexing/templating

Use Cases:
- Build a Claude-based red team assistant that loads domain-specific tactics on demand
- Standardize engagement methodology (checklists, escalation paths, reporting structure)
- Rapid triage and hypothesis generation for bug bounty findings (web/API/auth)
- Operator training/CTF prep with structured attack workflows per category
- Create/extend internal prompt libraries using the provided contribution template and manifest tooling

Keywords:
Claude Skills, SKILL.md, system prompt, red team playbooks, OWASP Top 10, SQL injection, XSS, SSRF, Active Directory, ADCS ESC1-15, Kerberoasting, NTLM relay, EDR evasion, indirect syscalls, PPID spoofing, exploit development, ROP, ASLR, CFG, CET, fuzzing, AFL++, libFuzzer, Kubernetes attacks, container escape, WPA2, WPA3-SAE, 802.1X EAP, BLE, Zigbee, Z-Wave, LoRaWAN, CI/CD exploitation, GitHub Actions, prompt injection, RAG poisoning